[Retroactive note added later, per the Symptom/Ruled out/Root cause/Fix commit-message framework]

Symptom (reasoned preventively, not yet observed as a live crash report):
Step 4's runtime download and Step 7's installer wizard are both long,
unattended waits with no user interaction in between.

Root cause: unlike a browser download, neither `curl` nor Wine/Inno Setup
requests its own "stay awake" power assertion — a laptop that idles into
sleep mid-download or mid-install would stall with no clear indication
of why, easily misread as a hang or crash.

Fix: wrapped both waits in `caffeinate -i`, which holds the assertion
only as long as the wrapped command runs and releases automatically on exit.
